{
  "question_id": "q_074_user_retention",
  "slug": "user-retention",
  "title": "Active User Retention",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "Facebook",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "Assume you're given a table containing information on Facebook user actions. Write a query to obtain number of monthly active users (MAUs) in July 2022, including the month in numerical format \"1, 2, 3\".\n\nHint:",
  "notes": [
    "An active user is defined as a user who has performed actions such as 'sign-in', 'like', or 'comment' in both the current month and the previous month.",
    "In June 2022, there was only one monthly active user (MAU) with the user_id 445.",
    "Please note that the output provided is for June 2022 as the user_actions table only contains event dates for that month. You should adapt the solution accordingly for July 2022.",
    "The dataset you are querying against may have different input & output - this is just an example!"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "user_actions",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "user_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "event_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "event_type",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(50)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "event_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "user_actions": [
      {
        "user_id": 445,
        "event_id": 101,
        "event_type": "sign-in",
        "event_date": "2022-06-03 10:00:00"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 445,
        "event_id": 102,
